WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:02.202
A new wave of Russian strikes on Kiev.

00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:05.472
Ukraine says its air defense system
intercepted 36

00:00:05.472 --> 00:00:08.441
missiles and drones over the capital city
early Friday.

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:10.710
At least two people were injured.

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:12.145
Meanwhile, multiple explosions

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:16.116
have been reported in a Russian occupied
port city in southern Ukraine.

00:00:16.383 --> 00:00:19.886
A Ukrainian official
says Russian positions have been hit.

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:25.058
And this comes as Russian border
regions are struck by fresh attacks.

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:27.627
Sam Kiley joining us.

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:30.864
Sam, a new wave of these hits towards
Kiev.

00:00:31.131 --> 00:00:36.536
Many of these missiles intercepted
and frankly, a lot of activity in Russian

00:00:36.536 --> 00:00:40.440
occupied territories as well as what
we're seeing inside of Russia.

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:43.710
This week, there's been so much activity

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.014
Yes, Elena.

00:00:48.014 --> 00:00:53.019
What we've can see now is very obviously
a new campaign conducted by the Ukrainians

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:58.058
or on the behalf of the Ukrainians,
Ukrainians inside Russia.

00:00:58.058 --> 00:01:03.029
They're not taking any direct
responsibility for the invasion or raids

00:01:03.029 --> 00:01:06.833
being carried out by Russian nationals
who are badged

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:11.671
effectively to the Ukrainian armed forces
crossing into Belgorod region.

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:16.209
But that's just what they have done with
the local authorities in Russia, saying

00:01:16.443 --> 00:01:21.848
two people are being killed in a bombing
or mortar attacks in frontline villages.

00:01:21.848 --> 00:01:25.218
At the same time in Smolensk,
another Russian city

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:28.288
north of Kiev.

00:01:28.288 --> 00:01:32.192
The oil refinery has been hit by
what is assumed to be a drone attack

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:37.230
similar to the one that hit in Krasnodar
south of the country.

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:41.101
So there is a pattern emerging here
on top of the pattern

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:44.938
that is long preexisting,
which is the systematic targeting,

00:01:44.938 --> 00:01:50.777
particularly of key, particularly of
civilians by the Russians inside Ukraine.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.645
Now, this is having a strategic effect.

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:57.283
The campaign inside Russia,
with Vladimir Putin coming out today

00:01:57.517 --> 00:01:59.752
saying that essentially
I'm paraphrasing here,

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:03.523
we mustn't get rattled, we mustn't
allow them to destabilize Russia.

00:02:03.523 --> 00:02:04.657
But that's exactly

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:09.062
what these relatively small scale attacks
inside Russian territory

00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:14.501
are intended to do to destabilize
the Russian effort with Ukraine.

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:17.971
Making all kinds of claims about
the movement of Russian special forces

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:21.741
into that area, which are unverifiable
but again, are intended

00:02:22.275 --> 00:02:26.212
whether they're true or false,
to sow unease, discomfort

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:30.984
and dismay among the Russian forces
as they continue to threaten to prosecute

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:36.322
a campaign, a counter offensive inside
Ukraine to recapture lost territory.

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:39.859
But I think we should see these campaigns
inside Russian territory

00:02:40.026 --> 00:02:42.695
as the early stages
of their counter offensive

00:02:45.732 --> 00:02:46.933
Sam Kiley, great to have you on.

00:02:46.933 --> 00:02:48.168
Thank you so much.

00:02:48.168 --> 00:02:51.171
And we're now joined by Timothy Miller,
one off.

00:02:51.171 --> 00:02:52.305
He is the president

00:02:52.305 --> 00:02:56.743
of the Keefe School of Economics, and
he is coming to us right now from Kiev.

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:58.878
It's very nice to see you.

00:02:58.878 --> 00:03:02.682
And we want to try and get the measure
of what it's been like the last

00:03:02.682 --> 00:03:07.253
few nights, especially as Russia continues
its assault.

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:09.722
I mean, could you ever imagine

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:12.325
that you and your fellow citizens
would be under this kind of siege

00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:14.761
now almost a year and a half
after this invasion began?

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:18.264
Yeah, when the start when the war started,

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:21.367
I would all hope that would end first.

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:25.471
But several months into the war, you know,
I think

00:03:26.039 --> 00:03:30.510
too many of us came
a realization that might go on forever.

00:03:30.677 --> 00:03:33.646
And we know how brutal Russia is,

00:03:33.646 --> 00:03:37.717
especially after the early revelation
and butcher and car.

00:03:38.218 --> 00:03:41.688
So I'm not surprised they're trying
to target civilians with missiles.

00:03:41.988 --> 00:03:46.025
But let me tell you, this last month
was really, really difficult.

00:03:46.025 --> 00:03:48.361
I think everyone cannot sleep.

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:50.396
Everyone is traumatized.

00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:55.201
We have been through maybe 18,
19 attacks in the last 30, 32 days.

00:03:55.835 --> 00:03:57.770
This is brutal every night.

00:03:57.770 --> 00:04:00.607
I expect to be awake at 3 a.m.

00:04:01.274 --> 00:04:03.576
being afraid of missiles.

00:04:03.576 --> 00:04:03.810
Yeah.

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:07.180
And I can imagine when you're dealing
with all of that after so many months,

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:09.115
and then some people are in their home

00:04:09.115 --> 00:04:11.985
with young children,
with elderly, with disabled people.

00:04:12.252 --> 00:04:16.456
It must just strike terror in so many
people, night after night after night.

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:18.992
It strikes

00:04:18.992 --> 00:04:21.995
maybe not terror, but fear fear

00:04:21.995 --> 00:04:25.498
for the loved ones and excuse me.

00:04:25.732 --> 00:04:27.967
And then anger at Russia.

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:31.170
Now, you argue

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:34.607
that Ukraine needs to prosecute this war
itself.

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:35.475
Defend itself.

00:04:35.475 --> 00:04:39.512
But, you know, you kind of are saying
in a way, and you have been for months now

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:42.315
that Ukraine cannot submit
to this state of war.

00:04:42.315 --> 00:04:43.116
For one thing,

00:04:43.116 --> 00:04:47.253
you've been advocating that the rebuilding
should actually start now. Why?

00:04:47.287 --> 00:04:47.687
I mean,

00:04:47.687 --> 00:04:51.090
you can understand the reluctance, right,
of international partners who are saying

00:04:51.457 --> 00:04:54.727
you know, especially under the barrage
that you've had the last few weeks,

00:04:54.727 --> 00:04:58.431
this is not a good time
to think about rebuilding the country.

00:04:59.599 --> 00:05:02.535
Well, that's because when people are far

00:05:02.702 --> 00:05:06.973
from the situation itself,
they tend to simplify.

00:05:07.006 --> 00:05:10.777
They simply don't have enough context,
enough visuals and not emotions.

00:05:11.044 --> 00:05:12.478
For them, it's a war.

00:05:12.478 --> 00:05:15.181
And then there will be at the end
of the war and then we will rebuild.

00:05:15.548 --> 00:05:18.518
But on the ground
is something very different.

00:05:18.551 --> 00:05:21.287
You have a clinic.
Clinic has been destroyed.

00:05:21.487 --> 00:05:23.523
People have to continue to get care.

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:26.192
For example, cancer
patients have to get treatment.

00:05:26.192 --> 00:05:26.759
Otherwise, what?

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:27.760
They will die.

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:30.096
People with heart attacks
have to get treatment.

00:05:30.096 --> 00:05:33.333
And brought to the hospitals quickly
in time to be safe.

00:05:33.566 --> 00:05:35.668
So we need those facilities now.

00:05:35.668 --> 00:05:40.473
When we talk about recovery
during the war, we actually not talking

00:05:40.473 --> 00:05:45.178
about rebuilding some kind of grand vision
of the future of Ukraine during the war.

00:05:45.345 --> 00:05:49.082
But we are talking about maintaining
the economy, maintaining the resilience,

00:05:49.282 --> 00:05:52.852
providing people
with services that they need right now.

00:05:54.854 --> 00:05:55.588
You know,

00:05:55.922 --> 00:05:57.790
one of
the ways that you've been communicating

00:05:57.790 --> 00:06:00.993
with other people in Ukraine,
but mostly the world or your Twitter feeds

00:06:00.993 --> 00:06:05.631
and you always gives such an intimate view
of your life there during wartime.

00:06:06.032 --> 00:06:09.869
I want to talk about what you posted
recently because it took many by surprise.

00:06:10.336 --> 00:06:15.208
You know, it was just video phone
video of a normal day at the McDonald's.

00:06:15.208 --> 00:06:16.175
You can see it there.

00:06:16.175 --> 00:06:17.577
You're walking with the phone.

00:06:17.577 --> 00:06:20.213
10 million people viewed it.

00:06:20.913 --> 00:06:23.216
What do you make of the reaction

00:06:23.683 --> 00:06:25.785
that you got from this?

00:06:26.352 --> 00:06:28.421
The reaction, quote, was polarizing.

00:06:28.855 --> 00:06:31.924
Some people said, listen, this is great.

00:06:31.924 --> 00:06:33.292
Ukraine is resilient.

00:06:33.292 --> 00:06:35.194
This is another example that they're like

00:06:35.194 --> 00:06:38.965
cos they continue
to go about their lives as normal.

00:06:39.065 --> 00:06:40.533
And we have to support them.

00:06:40.533 --> 00:06:42.301
We stand with Ukraine.

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:46.672
But others said, listen, guys,
it looks like completely normal.

00:06:46.773 --> 00:06:48.141
There is no war.

00:06:48.141 --> 00:06:49.375
War is a fake.

00:06:49.375 --> 00:06:51.778
Don't send us our taxpayers money to it.

00:06:52.044 --> 00:06:55.014
And I engaged with
some of the people on Twitter,

00:06:55.114 --> 00:06:59.318
and some of them are very, very anti
Ukrainian and pro-Russian people.

00:06:59.452 --> 00:07:01.587
And we talked privately and publicly.

00:07:01.754 --> 00:07:05.491
And I think they sort of slowly start
coming about

00:07:05.491 --> 00:07:09.362
because their impression is
then when there is a war

00:07:10.129 --> 00:07:14.500
that must be that everything is destroyed
and people are in shelters, all the time.

00:07:14.734 --> 00:07:18.971
But that's not how it is
when the attack stops.

00:07:19.272 --> 00:07:24.911
Kiev comes out to war or any city in
Ukraine, any village almost immediately.

00:07:25.111 --> 00:07:26.646
I think it's our point.

00:07:26.646 --> 00:07:30.383
We are trying to make this clear
that we will continue to war.

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:32.218
We will continue to leave.

00:07:32.218 --> 00:07:33.586
And this is our answer.

00:07:33.586 --> 00:07:35.788
Civil lands to the Russian terror.

00:07:35.822 --> 00:07:39.992
And I think it's sometimes difficult
to understand from afar,

00:07:40.526 --> 00:07:44.931
but I'm glad that some of my tweets
make this discussion public.

00:07:45.331 --> 00:07:45.631
Yeah.

00:07:45.631 --> 00:07:48.901
Going to McDonald's, getting ice cream,
sitting on some of those patios

00:07:48.901 --> 00:07:52.905
in Ukraine, its very own
form of resistance during this conflict.

00:07:53.072 --> 00:07:54.040
Timothy, thanks so much.

00:07:54.040 --> 00:07:56.442
Really appreciate you being with us.
And we'll continue to check in with you.

